              Black-Scholes calculates Greeks by taking analytical partial derivatives of the option pricing function V(S, t, &sigma;, r, K) with respect to each underlying variable. Delta is &part;V/&part;S, Gamma is &part;<sup>2</sup>V/&part;S<sup>2</sup>, Vega is &part;V/&part;&sigma;, Theta is &part;V/&part;t, and Rho is &part;V/&part;r. Because closed-form formulas exist, calculations execute instantaneously in client-side code without numerical discretization error.
